WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.080
- Kelly always wraps up the
show with something cool

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.810
from social media to bring you a smile.

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:07.400
Now it's my turn.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.280
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.413
(dramatic music)

00:00:11.413 --> 00:00:12.880
(audience clapping)

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:16.150
Lots of little kids are scared
of going in for a haircut,

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:19.610
but it's always been an
especially terrifying experience

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:21.350
for six year-old Jackson.

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:24.130
Jackson is autistic and
usually his mum Laquista

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:25.790
brings headphones and snacks

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:27.640
to keep him distracted during cuts.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:31.350
Now, one day Laquista forgot
to bring headphones or food.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:34.240
So when she got to the
barber, she had no idea

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.720
if Jackson could handle
sitting in the chair.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.800
That's when their barber Ree,
masterfully took control.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.990
By the end, Jackson was
having a grand whole time.

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:44.823
Take a look.

00:00:44.823 --> 00:00:47.336
(upbeat music)

00:01:04.953 --> 00:01:07.142
(audience clapping)

00:01:07.142 --> 00:01:09.240
Let's say hello to Laquista Jackson

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.341
and their miracle worker, barber Ree.

00:01:11.341 --> 00:01:13.930
(audience clapping)

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:16.180
Wow, hey, how are you guys?

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:17.580
What, that day had already been,

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:20.920
especially challenging
before getting to Ree, right?

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:22.490
How was that?

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:26.850
- Right there, so the day
started out just really bad.

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:31.050
We woke up late that day
and got caught in traffic.

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:35.090
So I forgot his headphones,
we didn't have time for lunch.

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:37.500
So by the time we got to the shop,

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.290
everybody was already kinda anxious.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:44.130
And so my oldest son, he
goes in to get his haircut

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:46.180
and now it's Jackson's turn

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:49.680
and he absolutely refused
to sit in the seat.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.930
So Ree is trying to put the cape on him

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:54.250
and he's blocking everything.

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:58.100
And so Ree looks at me
and she's like, I got you,

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:00.100
in her little calm voice.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:00.933
- I love that.

00:02:00.933 --> 00:02:03.500
- And I just sat back and
I'm like, you know what?

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.520
She's never gonna be able to cut his hair.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:09.250
But I peep out of the corner of my eye

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:11.120
and she's actually cutting his hair

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:13.270
while he's running around the shop.

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:14.103
- Wow.

00:02:14.103 --> 00:02:18.290
- Ree is really been
heaven sent to our family,

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:21.100
she's built this great
relationship with Jackson

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.670
and he asked me, trust her.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:25.050
So we thank her so much

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:28.040
and he actually looks forward
to getting his hair cut.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:29.680
- That's amazing, I love that.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.010
And Ree you say you were determined

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.980
to make a good day for Jackson.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:35.960
What was that like?

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:37.713
I mean, what gave you the idea?

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:40.900
- Absolutely, I was determined.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:44.410
My goal was to complete Jackson's haircut.

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:46.100
When they came into the shop,

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:49.020
I could tell they weren't
having a great day,

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:53.100
but I know my guy Jackson
loves games, he loves games.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.220
So I noticed his shirt,

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:57.800
he had Mario on his shirt
and Mario on the sofa.

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:00.390
So I told him we had to
protect Mario on his shirt

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:02.660
because the Mario on the
sofa was gonna attack us

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:06.160
and to complete the haircut.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:08.500
I felt like it would distract him.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.820
So the haircut turned out
good, everything went great.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.000
And I felt good, I felt accomplished

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.040
to see them leave out the shop happy.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:19.050
- Oh my goodness, it is such
a great thing that you did.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:21.820
And I'm like you guys as
you're posed right now.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:22.770
Thank you.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:25.420
Right, that's not all,
our season long partner,

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:27.310
Pilot Pen Makers of Frixion,

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:30.230
the go-to erasable pen of
the Kelly Clarkson show,

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:34.270
wants to celebrate those creating
fearlessly, just like you.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:37.070
So they're giving you $1,000,

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:39.920
that's 500 for Ree and 500 for Laquista.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:41.601
So congratulations
guys, thank you so much.

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:43.026
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

00:03:43.026 --> 00:03:43.859
- Thank you,

00:03:43.859 --> 00:03:44.868
- Thank you.

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:45.701
- Say thank you Jack.

00:03:45.701 --> 00:03:46.534
- Thank you.

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:49.603
- Thank you Bud, I love it.

